Research progress on SNO-modified proteins in cancer
SNO modification plays an important role in protein stability and catalytic activity, and it significantly impacts the survival and death of tumor cells [
110
,
111
]. The functions of SNO-modified proteins in various cancers are listed in Table
2
. The SNO modification of signaling pathway proteins can determine the outcome of various cancers, such as lung cancer, colorectal cancer, breast cancer, liver cancer, and ovarian cancer [
112
–
114
]. In addition, SNO modifications of different proteins have fundamentally different effects on cancer cells, implying that a general increase or decrease in SNO modifications cannot completely determine the outcome of all cancers [
113
]. Detailed analysis is needed to understand the impact of a single SNO-modified protein on specific cancer types.
